---
import { Code } from "astro:components";
import Base from "../../layouts/Base.astro";

// The site's greys, with the warm and teal accents of its ASCII banners.
const theme = {
  name: "jacques-mono",
  type: "dark",
  colors: { "editor.background": "#0c0c0c", "editor.foreground": "#d6d4cf" },
  tokenColors: [
    { settings: { foreground: "#d6d4cf" } },
    { scope: ["comment", "punctuation.definition.comment"], settings: { foreground: "#5e5e5e", fontStyle: "italic" } },
    { scope: ["keyword", "storage", "storage.type", "keyword.control"], settings: { foreground: "#ffffff" } },
    { scope: ["string", "string.quoted", "punctuation.definition.string"], settings: { foreground: "#6fbfb0" } },
    { scope: ["constant.numeric", "constant.language"], settings: { foreground: "#e0914f" } },
    { scope: ["entity.name.function", "support.function", "meta.function-call entity.name.function"], settings: { foreground: "#ffffff" } },
    { scope: ["entity.name.type", "support.class", "entity.name.class", "variable.other.constant"], settings: { foreground: "#e0914f" } },
    { scope: ["meta.object-literal.key", "support.type.property-name", "variable.other.property"], settings: { foreground: "#a8a6a1" } },
    { scope: ["punctuation", "meta.brace", "keyword.operator"], settings: { foreground: "#7a7a7a" } },
  ],
};

const code = `const model = await Decision.load(url);
const { answers } = await model.systemOne(ticket, {
  topic: { type: "choice", instructions: "What is the topic?",
           criteria: { billing: null, delivery: null } },
  churn: { type: "noul",   instructions: "Is the customer about to leave?" },
});
// answers.churn → { noul: 0.83 }`;

// token counts of a few packed questions (diagram 1); a static-shape engine pads each one to 136
const seqs = [104, 92, 118, 85, 121, 99, 110, 96];
const free = seqs.length * 136 - seqs.reduce((a, n) => a + n, 0); // room left on decision.js's row
---
<Base title="decision.js — Jacques" description="decision.js, an experiment: fast WebGPU inference for System One decision models, in the browser.">
  <main class="page">
    <p class="eyebrow">Experiment — WebGPU</p>
    <h1>decision.js</h1>
    <p class="lede">
      An experiment: how fast can a browser run <strong>System One</strong> models? These are small models that
      make quick decisions (yes / no, pick an option, give a score) instead of writing text. decision.js is a
      small WebGPU inference engine written from scratch for them.
    </p>
    <div class="cta">
      <a class="btn primary" href="/decision/playground">View playground →</a>
      <a class="btn" href="https://github.com/Jacqkues/decision.js">View code</a>
    </div>

    <figure class="flow" aria-label="A state and questions go into the model on the GPU, which returns a probability per option">
      <div class="inputs">
        <div class="node"><span class="k">State</span><span>a ticket, a form, any JSON</span></div>
        <div class="node"><span class="k">Questions</span><span>yes / no · choice · score</span></div>
      </div>
      <div class="arrow" aria-hidden="true"></div>
      <div class="node model"><span class="k">Model · WebGPU</span><span>d1 or d3-lite, one forward pass, no text generated</span></div>
      <div class="arrow" aria-hidden="true"></div>
      <div class="node out">
        <span class="k">Answers</span>
        <span class="bar"><i>delivery</i><b style="--w: 96%"></b><em>96%</em></span>
        <span class="bar"><i>billing</i><b style="--w: 3%"></b><em>3%</em></span>
        <span class="bar"><i>bug</i><b style="--w: 1%"></b><em>1%</em></span>
      </div>
    </figure>

    <div class="prose">
      <h2>So far</h2>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>34 ms</strong> for 3 decisions on a support ticket with d1-omni (Apple M5 Pro, Chrome).</li>
        <li>About <strong>2× faster</strong> than Google's LiteRT.js on the same model.</li>
        <li>Answers that <strong>match</strong> the models' official PyTorch code, and nothing leaves the page.</li>
      </ul>
      <Code code={code} lang="ts" theme={theme} />

      <h2>How it works</h2>

      <h3>1 · Every question in one pass, no padding</h3>
      <p>
        Each question becomes its own prompt. decision.js packs them end to end on one token axis and runs the
        whole batch as a single GPU command buffer; per-token metadata tells the attention which tokens belong
        together. Engines with static shapes pad every prompt to a fixed length instead.
      </p>
    </div>
    <figure class="diagram pack">
      <div class="lane"><span class="lane-k">decision.js</span><div class="row">{seqs.map((n, i) => <span class="seq" style={`flex: ${n}`}>{i < 3 ? `q${i + 1}` : ""}</span>)}<span class="rest" style={`flex: ${free}`}></span></div></div>
      <div class="lane"><span class="lane-k">static shapes</span><div class="row">{seqs.map((n) => <span class="seq padded" style={`flex: 136; --real: ${(100 * n) / 136}%`}></span>)}</div></div>
      <figcaption>Same questions, same width per token. On d1-omni, padding was about a quarter of LiteRT.js's work.</figcaption>
    </figure>

    <div class="prose">
      <h3>2 · Weights converted once, then straight to the matrix units</h3>
      <p>
        The weights ship as 8-bit (half the download). At load time a GPU kernel turns them into f16 laid out in
        8×8 blocks, the shape the GPU's matrix units read, so the matrix multiplication loads them directly
        with no dequantization in the hot loop (the design of Google's ML Drift).
      </p>
    </div>
    <figure class="diagram flow-x">
      <div class="node"><span class="k">weights.bin</span><span>q8 · 803 MB<br />Hugging Face, cached</span></div>
      <div class="arrow" aria-hidden="true"></div>
      <div class="node"><span class="k">Once, at load</span><span>q8 → f16<br />8×8 blocks</span></div>
      <div class="arrow" aria-hidden="true"></div>
      <div class="node model"><span class="k">Matmul</span><span>subgroup matrices<br />≈ 93% of the chip's peak</span></div>
    </figure>

    <div class="prose">
      <h3>3 · Where the time goes</h3>
      <p>
        Once the matrix multiplications run near the hardware's limit, everything else is small, so it is fused:
        each d3-lite DeltaNet layer (convolution, norms, gates, the recurrence and the gated norm) is a single
        kernel, and the MLP's activation runs inside its matmul.
      </p>
    </div>
    <figure class="diagram time">
      <div class="stack" role="img" aria-label="GPU time per d3-lite ticket: matrix multiplications about 86%, DeltaNet kernel about 8%, attention about 4%, the rest about 2%">
        <span class="seg mm" style="flex: 86">matmuls · 86%</span>
        <span class="seg dn" style="flex: 8"></span>
        <span class="seg at" style="flex: 4"></span>
        <span class="seg ot" style="flex: 2"></span>
      </div>
      <div class="legend">
        <span><i class="mm"></i>matrix multiplications</span>
        <span><i class="dn"></i>DeltaNet kernel · 8%</span>
        <span><i class="at"></i>attention · 4%</span>
        <span><i class="ot"></i>the rest · 2%</span>
      </div>
      <figcaption>GPU time of one d3-lite ticket (3 questions), kernel by kernel.</figcaption>
    </figure>

    <div class="prose">
      <h3>4 · Only the options are scored</h3>
      <p>
        A chat model would compute a score for every word of its vocabulary at every step. A decision needs one
        step and a few candidates: decision.js reads the hidden state at the answer position and scores only the
        options' codes.
      </p>
    </div>
    <figure class="diagram flow-x">
      <div class="node"><span class="k">Last token</span><span>hidden state<br />1,024 values</span></div>
      <div class="arrow" aria-hidden="true"></div>
      <div class="node model"><span class="k">3 dot products</span><span>A · B · C<br />not 248,320 words</span></div>
      <div class="arrow" aria-hidden="true"></div>
      <div class="node out">
        <span class="k">Softmax</span>
        <span class="bar"><i>A</i><b style="--w: 96%"></b><em>96%</em></span>
        <span class="bar"><i>B</i><b style="--w: 3%"></b><em>3%</em></span>
        <span class="bar"><i>C</i><b style="--w: 1%"></b><em>1%</em></span>
      </div>
    </figure>
  </main>
</Base>

<style>
  .page { max-width: 52rem; }
  h1 { font-size: clamp(2.4rem, 6vw, 3.6rem); letter-spacing: -0.02em; }
  .lede { color: #d6d4cf; font-size: 1rem; margin: 1rem 0 2rem; max-width: 42rem; }
  .lede strong { color: var(--ink); font-weight: 300; }

  .cta { display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 0.7rem; }
  .btn {
    font-size: 0.7rem; letter-spacing: 0.18em; text-transform: uppercase;
    padding: 0.95rem 1.5rem; border: 1px solid var(--dim); color: var(--ink);
    transition: color 0.2s, background 0.2s, border-color 0.2s;
  }
  .btn:hover { border-color: var(--ink); background: #161616; }
  .btn.primary { background: var(--ink); color: var(--bg); border-color: var(--ink); }
  .btn.primary:hover { background: transparent; color: var(--ink); }

  /* the diagram: inputs → model → answers, stacked on small screens */
  .flow { margin: 3.5rem 0 1rem; display: grid; grid-template-columns: 1fr auto 1fr auto 1fr; align-items: center; gap: 0; }
  .inputs { display: grid; gap: 0.6rem; }
  .node { border: 1px solid var(--subtle); padding: 0.8rem 0.9rem; display: grid; gap: 0.3rem; font-size: 0.78rem; color: var(--dim); background: #070707; }
  .k { font-size: 0.6rem; letter-spacing: 0.2em; text-transform: uppercase; color: var(--ink); }
  .model { border-color: #e0914f; }
  .model .k { color: #e0914f; }
  .arrow { width: 2.2rem; height: 1px; background: var(--subtle); position: relative; }
  .arrow::after { content: ""; position: absolute; right: -1px; top: -3px; border: 3.5px solid transparent; border-left: 6px solid var(--subtle); border-right: 0; }
  .bar { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 4.2rem 1fr 2.4rem; gap: 0.5rem; align-items: center; }
  .bar i { font-style: normal; }
  .bar b { height: 2px; background: linear-gradient(90deg, var(--ink) var(--w), var(--line) var(--w)); }
  .bar em { font-style: normal; text-align: right; font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums; }
  .bar:nth-of-type(2) { color: var(--ink); }
  @media (max-width: 46rem) {
    .flow { grid-template-columns: 1fr; justify-items: stretch; }
    .arrow { width: 1px; height: 1.6rem; justify-self: center; }
    .arrow::after { right: -3px; top: auto; bottom: -1px; border: 3.5px solid transparent; border-top: 6px solid var(--subtle); border-bottom: 0; }
  }

  .prose { margin-top: 1rem; }
  .prose h3 { font-size: 0.95rem; color: var(--ink); margin: 2.4rem 0 0.6rem; }

  .diagram { margin: 1.4rem 0 0.6rem; }
  .diagram figcaption { margin-top: 0.7rem; font-size: 0.72rem; color: var(--subtle); }

  /* 1 · packing */
  .lane { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 7.5rem 1fr; gap: 0.8rem; align-items: center; margin-bottom: 0.5rem; }
  .lane-k { font-size: 0.6rem; letter-spacing: 0.18em; text-transform: uppercase; color: var(--dim); }
  .row { display: flex; gap: 2px; height: 1.6rem; }
  .seq { background: #2e2e2e; font-size: 0.6rem; color: var(--ink); display: flex; align-items: center; padding-left: 0.35rem; min-width: 0; overflow: hidden; }
  .seq:nth-child(odd) { background: #4a4a4a; }
  .rest { border: 1px dashed var(--line); }
  .seq.padded { background: linear-gradient(90deg, #4a4a4a var(--real), transparent var(--real)), repeating-linear-gradient(135deg, #1c1c1c 0 3px, #0a0a0a 3px 6px); }
  @media (max-width: 40rem) { .lane { grid-template-columns: 1fr; gap: 0.3rem; } }

  /* 2 & 4 · pipelines */
  .flow-x { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 1fr auto 1fr auto 1fr; align-items: stretch; }
  .flow-x .arrow { align-self: center; }
  @media (max-width: 46rem) {
    .flow-x { grid-template-columns: 1fr; }
    .flow-x .arrow { width: 1px; height: 1.6rem; justify-self: center; }
    .flow-x .arrow::after { right: -3px; top: auto; bottom: -1px; border: 3.5px solid transparent; border-top: 6px solid var(--subtle); border-bottom: 0; }
  }

  /* 3 · time */
  .stack { display: flex; height: 2rem; gap: 2px; }
  .seg { display: flex; align-items: center; padding-left: 0.6rem; font-size: 0.66rem; letter-spacing: 0.1em; text-transform: uppercase; white-space: nowrap; overflow: hidden; }
  .mm { background: #e0914f; color: var(--bg); }
  .dn { background: #6fbfb0; }
  .at { background: #9a9a9a; }
  .ot { background: #4d4d4d; }
  .legend { display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 0.4rem 1.2rem; margin-top: 0.7rem; font-size: 0.72rem; color: var(--dim); }
  .legend i { display: inline-block; width: 0.6rem; height: 0.6rem; margin-right: 0.45rem; vertical-align: -0.05rem; }
  .prose :global(pre.astro-code) { background: #0c0c0c !important; }
</style>
